      "message": "No, its not new options, its already there in common code \"include/config.h\"\n\n/*\n * Here are some recommended color settings by default, but a board can change\n * the colors to one of \"enum ec_led_colors\" as they see fit.\n */\n#define CONFIG_LED_PWM_CHARGE_COLOR EC_LED_COLOR_AMBER\n#define CONFIG_LED_PWM_NEAR_FULL_COLOR EC_LED_COLOR_GREEN\n#define CONFIG_LED_PWM_CHARGE_ERROR_COLOR EC_LED_COLOR_RED\n#define CONFIG_LED_PWM_SOC_ON_COLOR EC_LED_COLOR_GREEN\n#define CONFIG_LED_PWM_SOC_SUSPEND_COLOR EC_LED_COLOR_GREEN\n#define CONFIG_LED_PWM_LOW_BATT_COLOR EC_LED_COLOR_AMBER\n\n/*\n\nI added all options in zephyr conf, so that if any platform wants to override, they can.\n\nIn brya we are overriding only 4:\n#define CONFIG_LED_PWM_NEAR_FULL_COLOR EC_LED_COLOR_WHITE\n#define CONFIG_LED_PWM_SOC_ON_COLOR EC_LED_COLOR_WHITE\n#define CONFIG_LED_PWM_SOC_SUSPEND_COLOR EC_LED_COLOR_WHITE\n#define CONFIG_LED_PWM_LOW_BATT_COLOR EC_LED_COLOR_AMBER\n\nIn zepyr we are overriding this in CL: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/3322174",
